    <article class="legal-body">
      <header class="legal-head">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">
          Version <%= versao %> · Updated on <%= atualizadoEm %>
        </p>
        <p class="legal-lead">
          This policy explains what AquaTrip does with your personal data:
          what we collect, on what legal grounds, who we share it with, and
          how you control all of it. It is written to be understood without
          a lawyer at your side.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section id="quem">
        <h2>1. Who processes your data</h2>
        <p>
          AquaTrip is the platform where you find and book water
          experiences. We act as the <strong>controller</strong> of
          sign-up, browsing, and booking data.
        </p>
        <p>
          Whoever runs the experience (the partner responsible for each
          activity) is an independent controller with respect to the data
          they need to provide the service — for example, your name and the
          number of people on the day of the activity.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="dados">
        <h2>2. What we collect</h2>

        <h3>What you provide directly</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Sign-up:</strong> name and email.</li>
          <li><strong>Password:</strong> stored only as a cryptographic hash (Argon2id). We do not have access to your password and cannot recover it — only let you create a new one.</li>
          <li><strong>Bookings:</strong> the experience chosen, date, time, and number of people.</li>
          <li><strong>Contact:</strong> whatever you write when reaching out to us.</li>
          <li><strong>Reviews:</strong> the rating and text you publish about an experience you took. These remain
            <strong>public</strong>, signed only with your first name and last initial (e.g., "Lia S.").
            You may delete them whenever you like.</li>
          <li><strong>Review photos:</strong> up to 3 per review. Before saving, we automatically strip
            hidden data from the file — including the <strong>location (GPS)</strong>
            that phones embed in photos. Each photo goes through team review and only becomes public if it is
            approved. A rejected photo is deleted, and you receive the reason by email.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Collected automatically</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Access logs:</strong> IP address, date and time, and the action taken (login, booking, payment). We keep this for security and to be able to investigate incidents.</li>
          <li><strong>Session:</strong> a cookie that keeps you logged in.</li>
          <li><strong>Preferences:</strong> light/dark theme and recent searches, stored in your own browser.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What we do not collect</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Card number, security code, or expiration date — that data goes from your browser straight to the payment provider and <strong>never passes through our servers</strong>.</li>
          <li>Your precise location.</li>
          <li>Sensitive data (racial or ethnic origin, religious belief, political opinion, health, biometrics).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="parceiros">
        <h2>2.1. If you are a partner (offering experiences)</h2>
        <p>For those who register as a partner, we also process:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>CPF or CNPJ, full name or company name:</strong> to identify who provides the service
            and to comply with tax obligations. <strong>The CPF (Brazilian individual taxpayer ID) is never displayed publicly</strong> and appears
            masked on screen, except to our team during registration review.</li>
          <li><strong>Phone, city, and state:</strong> so our team can reach you. The phone number is not shown to customers.</li>
          <li><strong>Display name:</strong> this is public — it appears on your experiences.</li>
          <li><strong>Mercado Pago connection:</strong> when you connect your account to receive payouts, we store
            the access credentials encrypted; we do not have access to your Mercado Pago password.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="legal-note">
          Legal basis: performance of the partnership contract and compliance with a legal obligation (LGPD art. 7, items II and V).
          As long as there are experiences and sales tied to your registration, deleting the account depends on
          the formal termination of the partnership, due to the legal duty to keep sales records for tax purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="bases">
        <h2>3. Why we can process your data</h2>
        <p>
          The LGPD (Lei Geral de Proteção de Dados, Brazil's data protection law) requires a legal basis for each purpose. Ours are:
        </p>
        <div class="legal-table-wrap">
          <table class="legal-table">
            <caption class="sr-only">Legal bases by processing purpose</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Legal basis</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Creating and maintaining your account</td><td>Contract performance (art. 7, V)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Processing bookings and payment</td><td>Contract performance (art. 7, V)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Sending account emails (confirmation, password reset, receipt)</td><td>Contract performance (art. 7, V)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Access logs and security</td><td>Legal obligation (Marco Civil da Internet, art. 15) and legitimate interest (art. 7, IX)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Retention of payment tax records</td><td>Legal obligation (art. 7, II)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Usage metrics</td><td><strong>Consent</strong> (art. 7, I) — optional</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Marketing communications</td><td><strong>Consent</strong> (art. 7, I) — optional</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="legal-note">
          The last two rows are the only ones that depend on your authorization.
          Declining them does not affect your ability to use the platform, book, or pay.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="cookies">
        <h2>4. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
        <div class="legal-table-wrap">
          <table class="legal-table">
            <caption class="sr-only">Cookies used</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Category</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>aquatrip.sid</code></td><td>Keeps you logged in and protects forms against CSRF</td><td>Necessary</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>aquatrip_theme</code></td><td>Remembers whether you chose light or dark theme</td><td>Necessary</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>aquatrip_recent_searches</code></td><td>Your recent searches (stays only in your browser)</td><td>Necessary</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          Necessary cookies do not require consent because the service does
          not work without them. Should we ever use metrics or marketing
          cookies, they will only be activated <strong>after</strong> your
          explicit authorization — and you can revoke it at any time in the
          <a href="/configuracoes/privacidade">Privacy Center</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="compartilhamento">
        <h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Payment provider:</strong> receives the data needed to process the charge. It is the provider that handles your card data.</li>
          <li><strong>Experience partner:</strong> receives your name and booking details to run the activity.</li>
          <li><strong>Email provider:</strong> delivers transactional messages.</li>
          <li><strong>Infrastructure:</strong> hosting and database services.</li>
          <li><strong>Authorities:</strong> when required by a court order or legal obligation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="legal-note">
          <strong>We do not sell your data</strong> and we do not pass it on
          to third-party advertisers.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you open any AquaTrip page, your browser makes no request to
          third-party domains: fonts, icons, and scripts are all served by
          AquaTrip itself. This keeps your IP address from being shared with
          other companies just because you visited the site.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you want the current, complete list of these providers, request
          it through the Privacy Center — the list is updated according to
          our active contracts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="pagamento">
        <h2>6. Payment data</h2>
        <p>
          This point deserves its own section because it tends to raise
          questions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your card number, security code, and expiration date
          <strong>never travel through AquaTrip</strong>. They go from your
          browser directly to the payment provider, which returns a
          reference code. That code, along with the last four digits and the
          card brand, is what we store — enough for you to recognize the
          purchase, not enough for any charge.
        </p>
        <p>
          For PIX payments, we store only the charge identifier generated by
          the provider.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="retencao">
        <h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
        <div class="legal-table-wrap">
          <table class="legal-table">
            <caption class="sr-only">Retention periods</caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Data</th><th scope="col">Period</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Account and registration</td><td>As long as the account exists</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Bookings and payments</td><td>5 years after the transaction (tax and statute-of-limitations period)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Access logs</td><td>6 months (Marco Civil da Internet, art. 15)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Consent records</td><td>As long as the processing lasts, plus 5 years (as evidence)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Email and password tokens</td><td>Until used or expired; cleared after 7 days</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Messages sent through the contact form</td><td>As long as needed to respond and follow up. You may request deletion at any time.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="legal-note">
          For that reason, requesting account deletion does not erase your
          payment history: there is a legal obligation to retain it. What we
          do is <strong>anonymize</strong> it: your name and email are
          removed, your travel journal and contact messages are deleted, and
          the payment records that must be kept stop pointing to you. The
          confirmation reaches your email before this happens — after that,
          the address no longer exists in the system.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="seguranca">
        <h2>8. How we protect it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Passwords hashed with Argon2id — we do not store the password itself.</li>
          <li>Encrypted connection and security headers (CSP, HSTS).</li>
          <li>Account lockout after repeated failed login attempts.</li>
          <li>Audit trail of sensitive actions, with minimized data.</li>
          <li>Administrative access restricted by role and logged.</li>
          <li>Email links with short validity and single use.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="legal-note">
          No system is unbreakable. In the event of an incident with
          meaningful risk, we will notify you and the ANPD (Autoridade
          Nacional de Proteção de Dados, Brazil's National Data Protection
          Authority) as required by LGPD art. 48.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="direitos">
        <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
        <p>At any time, you may:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Confirm whether we process your data and access it</li>
          <li>Correct incomplete or outdated data</li>
          <li>Request anonymization, blocking, or deletion of unnecessary data</li>
          <li>Request portability</li>
          <li>Find out who we share your data with</li>
          <li>Withdraw consent</li>
          <li>Object to processing based on legitimate interest</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <a class="btn-primary" href="/configuracoes/privacidade">Go to the Privacy Center</a>
        </p>
        <p class="legal-note">
          Access and portability requests are handled instantly: you
          download a file with everything we have. Other requests are
          logged and answered within 15 days.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="menores">
        <h2>10. Children and teenagers</h2>
        <p>
          The platform is intended for people 18 and older. We do not
          knowingly collect data from minors without the specific consent of
          at least one parent or legal guardian (LGPD art. 14). If we
          identify such a case, we delete the data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="mudancas">
        <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          This policy carries a version number. When we change something
          that affects your choices, the version number increases and the
          consent notice appears again — because your earlier authorization
          was given to a different text. The history of your decisions
          stays in the Privacy Center.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contato">
        <h2>12. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Data Protection Officer (DPO):
          <a href="mailto:<%= encarregado %>"><%= encarregado %></a>
        </p>
        <p>
          You may also file a complaint with the ANPD (Autoridade Nacional
          de Proteção de Dados, Brazil's National Data Protection
          Authority).
        </p>
      </section>

      <aside class="legal-disclaimer">
        <strong>Note about this document</strong>
        <p>
          This text accurately describes what the system actually does — it
          was written from the code's real behavior, not from a boilerplate
          template. Even so, it <strong>does not replace legal
          review</strong>. Before operating commercially, submit it to a
          lawyer, who will add the company's legal name, tax ID (CNPJ),
          address, and the contractual terms specific to your business.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </article>
